[Slow] この飛行機は、福岡から鹿児島へ行く予定で、およそ40人が乗る予定でした。

22
00:02:18,524 --> 00:02:24,860
[Host] The plane was going to fly from Fukuoka to Kagoshima, and about forty people were going to board it.

23
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:27,572
[Vocab] 予定

24
00:02:27,972 --> 00:02:32,867
[Host] It means a plan or schedule. Here it shows something was scheduled to happen.

25
00:02:33,467 --> 00:02:35,364
[Vocab] 乗る

26
00:02:35,764 --> 00:02:38,548
[Host] It means to ride, or to get on.

27
00:02:39,147 --> 00:02:47,716
[Slow] 出発の準備をしているとき、パイロットが小さい動物を見つけました。

28
00:02:48,515 --> 00:02:53,099
[Host] While they were getting ready to leave, a pilot found the small animal.

29
00:02:53,699 --> 00:02:56,123
[Vocab] 出発

30
00:02:56,524 --> 00:02:58,395
[Host] It means departure.

31
00:02:58,996 --> 00:03:01,156
[Vocab] 準備

32
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:04,412
[Host] It means preparation, or getting ready.

33
00:03:05,012 --> 00:03:07,243
[Vocab] 見つける

34
00:03:07,644 --> 00:03:09,659
[Host] It means to find something.

35
00:03:10,259 --> 00:03:18,539
[Slow] でも、動物はすぐに逃げて、どこにいるか、わからなくなりました。

36
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:23,300
[Host] But the animal quickly ran away, and nobody knew where it was.

37
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:26,012
[Vocab] 逃げる

38
00:03:26,412 --> 00:03:29,123
[Host] It means to run away, or to escape.

39
00:03:29,723 --> 00:03:36,731
[Slow] 動物が飛行機の中の電気の線をかむと、危ないです。

40
00:03:37,532 --> 00:03:42,716
[Host] If the animal bites the electric wires inside the plane, it is dangerous.

41
00:03:43,316 --> 00:03:45,475
[Vocab] 電気

42
00:03:45,876 --> 00:03:47,747
[Host] It means electricity.

43
00:03:48,348 --> 00:03:50,243
